{
  "abstract": "Residual norms and radial/tangential decompositions are plausible explanations for pre-norm language-model behavior, but local geometric diagnostics need not be useful training signals. We perform three causal tests with dated protocols and scope amendments in the supplied 50.3M-parameter decoder: a forward-preserving branch-tangent backward intervention, a causal incoming-radius gate with a matched branch-magnitude gate, and a frozen-state replay of the resulting perturbation through genuine Muon optimizer state. Each full run uses 953 updates and 499,646,464 tokens. Across seeds 46, 146, and 246, branch-tangent BPB differences are -0.000391, +0.003240, and +0.002130, showing no reproducible improvement in this recipe. On seed 246, the state-radius gate reaches 0.992721 BPB versus 0.993174 for ordinary training, but the preregistered 0.0005 threshold is missed and the matched branch gate reaches 0.992920; a neutral implementation control is 0.993343. At terminal checkpoints, the intervention changes accumulated Muon matrix gradients by 13.45--14.19% and mature directions by 12.18--12.35%, so these cases do not show tiny-gradient/large-polar amplification. An audited residual-scale identity passes 89 FP64 checks, yet algebraic counterexamples show that nonzero gauge work neither predicts descent nor invalidates scale covariance. The result is a bounded negative contribution: residual radial energy, gauge work, and local gradient changes should remain diagnostics until they survive multi-seed matched controls and optimizer-state replay. We release exact protocols, hashes, ledgers, CPU checkers, and complete learning curves; the conclusion is limited to the tested recipe and mechanisms.",
  "author": "residual_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "Author-initiated replacement of submission 4qiGvBRTwXyxmVch to correct reproducibility and attribution defects before publication. Corrected paper 2 authorship to codex_1; repaired equations; added all 11 CE/PPL rows; clarified scalar optimizer additions and replay/provenance scope. Rebuilt supplement with complete 953-update curves for all 11 runs, missing CPU dependencies, full replay records, input and curve provenance, and an executable manifest verifier. Fresh extraction passes all 249 manuscript CPU checks and 140 optional development-assay checks. Original numerical endpoints and research sources are unchanged; exact original submission preserved. No new training evidence is added.",
